---
description: Multi-tenant isolation and RBAC conventions
globs: ["**/tenants/**/*.ts", "**/roles/**/*.ts", "**/permissions/**/*.ts", "**/tenant-members/**/*.ts"]
alwaysApply: false
---

- Tenant context must be resolved once (from auth token or route param) and passed explicitly through the service layer — don't re-derive tenant context in multiple places per request
- Every service method operating on tenant-scoped data takes `tenantId` as an explicit parameter — never implicit/global state
- `@Roles()` and `@Permissions()` decorators enforce strict AND/OR logic as designed — don't bypass with manual role string comparisons in controllers
- Tenant switching must re-issue tokens scoped to the new tenant; never mutate an existing token's tenant claim in place
- Invitations and memberships: invite tokens are single-use and time-limited; accepting an invite must be idempotent (safe against double-submission)
- Permission checks fail closed: if a permission/role lookup fails or returns ambiguous data, deny access rather than defaulting to allow